Lab 10: Configure User Types in Automation Controller
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Create different user types (admin, standard, and read-only users) in Ansible Automation Controller • Assign users to appropriate teams with proper role-based access control • Configure and verify RBAC setup to ensure proper access permissions • Understand the security implications of different user roles in automation environments • Implement best practices for user management in enterprise automation platforms

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic understanding of Linux command line operations • Familiarity with web-based interfaces and navigation • Knowledge of user management concepts in enterprise systems • Understanding of role-based access control (RBAC) principles • Completed previous Ansible Automation Controller labs or equivalent experience

Required Knowledge Areas:
Basic authentication and authorization concepts
Understanding of teams and organizations in enterprise software
Familiarity with JSON and YAML formats
Basic networking concepts for web applications
Lab Environment Setup
