Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Users Cannot Login
Symptoms: Login fails with correct credentials

Solutions:

Verify user is active:

# Check user status in database
sudo docker exec -it awx_postgres psql -U awx -d awx -c "SELECT username, is_active FROM auth_user;"
Reset user password if needed through admin interface

Issue 2: Permissions Not Working
Symptoms: Users see resources they shouldn't access

Solutions:

Clear browser cache and cookies
Verify team assignments are correct
Check role assignments on resources
Issue 3: Teams Not Showing Proper Access
Symptoms: Team members don't inherit expected permissions

Solutions:

Verify organization membership
Check team role assignments
Restart AWX services:
sudo docker restart awx_web awx_task
Best Practices for User Management
Security Best Practices
Use strong passwords for all user accounts
Implement least privilege principle - give minimum required access
Regular audit of user permissions and team memberships
Use teams instead of individual permissions for easier management
Document role assignments and access requirements
Operational Best Practices
Create standardized naming conventions for users and teams
Use descriptive team names that reflect their purpose
Regular cleanup of inactive users and unused teams
Implement approval workflows for user creation and permission changes
Monitor user activity through audit logs
Conclusion
In this comprehensive lab, you have successfully:

• Created three different user types (admin, standard, and read-only) with appropriate access levels • Established team-based organization for better permission management • Implemented role-based access control (RBAC) to secure your Automation Controller environment • Verified proper access restrictions through hands-on testing with different user accounts • Learned troubleshooting techniques for common user management issues

Why This Matters
Enterprise Security: Proper user management is crucial for maintaining security in enterprise automation environments. By implementing RBAC, you ensure that users only have access to the resources they need for their job functions.

Compliance Requirements: Many organizations must meet regulatory compliance standards that require proper access controls and audit trails. The skills learned in this lab directly support these requirements.

Operational Efficiency: Team-based permission management scales better than individual user permissions, making it easier to manage large numbers of users and maintain consistent access policies.

Career Relevance: These skills are directly applicable to the Red Hat Certified Specialist in Managing Automation with Ansible Automation Platform exam and are highly valued in DevOps and automation engineering roles.

